It was called Married with Children.

00:12:15.639 --> 00:12:17.790
And the main star, his name is Al Bundy.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:21.560
And he would always talk about how he threw
four touchdowns in high school, when they

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:23.639
won the championships, and he was in his fifties.

00:12:23.639 --> 00:12:28.600
And everyone said, people who talk about high
school victories, they're Al Bundys.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:31.329
Don't talk about victories from 22 years ago.

00:12:31.329 --> 00:12:35.000
You've got to talk about your most recent
victories.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.389
No one cares about 16 years ago, unless if
you're a grandpa and you're telling your story

00:12:38.389 --> 00:12:41.540
to your grandkids, and that was 39 years ago.

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:46.000
If you're in the hunt today, building it and
competing, you've got to talk about your recent

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.889
victories that you have.

00:12:47.889 --> 00:12:51.040
#3: One of the ways you self-promote is you
build up other people.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.959
That's strange, because a lot of times people
think you self-promote by knocking other people

00:12:54.959 --> 00:12:58.079
down, and there may be some conflicting ideas
here because some of these people are experts

00:12:58.079 --> 00:13:00.269
at knocking the other people down, right?

00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:03.430
You say hey, Ali used to say you look like
a mummy.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.190
He looks like a mummy.

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:07.189
Right, when you hear Ali talk all this smack.

00:13:07.189 --> 00:13:09.509
He's the ugliest man I've ever met in my life.

00:13:09.509 --> 00:13:11.629
I've never met a man uglier than him, right?

00:13:11.629 --> 00:13:14.810
He would say all this type of stuff.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.399
Mayweather would try to do that.

00:13:16.399 --> 00:13:19.840
Jordan was very big when he was talking smack
in the game.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:25.000
But there's an element of you building other
people up while you're building your business.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.339
I remember when we were selling memberships
at Bally Total Fitness and I had just come

00:13:28.339 --> 00:13:33.649
to a new club at Bally's and everybody there
was accustomed to selling the memberships

00:13:33.649 --> 00:13:36.069
by bashing 24-Hour Fitness.

00:13:36.069 --> 00:13:38.589
They would bash 24-Hour-Fitness and I told
everybody, listen, stop.

00:13:38.589 --> 00:13:39.940
We're no longer bashing 24-Hour-Fitness.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:40.940
They said, "Why?"

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.810
I said, Let me explain why we're not going
to bash.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.410
Here's what we're going to be doing.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.790
So people would come in and I would say, so
let me ask you, how much do you know about

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.800
Bally Total Fitness and what other gyms are
you looking at?

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.959
Oh, you know what, I've looked at you guys
and at 24-Hour Fitness.

00:13:50.959 --> 00:13:52.730
What do you like about 24-Hour Fitness?

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.009
I like the fact that 24-Hour Fitness doesn't
have a contract.

00:13:55.009 --> 00:13:56.759
Okay, aside from that, what else is important?

00:13:56.759 --> 00:13:58.490
Is distance important to you?

00:13:58.490 --> 00:13:59.649
Well yes.

00:13:59.649 --> 00:14:03.749
What's closer to your house, Bally Total Fitness
or 24-Hour Fitness?"

00:14:03.749 --> 00:14:06.069
They would say, Well I live a block away from
Bally's.

00:14:06.069 --> 00:14:07.990
I said, "So how far is 24-Hour-Fitness from
you?"

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:08.990
Nine miles.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.850
How much of a drive does it take in traffic?

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:11.850
About 30 minutes.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.010
How long does it take to come over here?

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.029
They would say, "five minutes."

00:14:14.029 --> 00:14:17.079
I said, "So that's about 25 minutes difference
going and coming back.

00:14:17.079 --> 00:14:18.290
So that's 50 minutes, right?

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:22.379
I said, is 50 minutes times three times a
week that you're planning on coming to the

00:14:22.379 --> 00:14:28.089
gym, that's 150 minutes a week, 600 minutes
per month, is that worth more than $5 a month

00:14:28.089 --> 00:14:29.089
for you?

00:14:29.089 --> 00:14:31.589
And they would say, "Well, you know, it is."

00:14:31.589 --> 00:14:34.199
I said, "So you want to go to 24-Hour Fitness.

00:14:34.199 --> 00:14:39.740
And you're willing to give up 600 minutes
per month just for $5 less?

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:41.399
Just for no agreement?

00:14:41.399 --> 00:14:45.660
Isn't time more important to you than a price
on a down payment of a membership?"

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:46.660
Of course it is.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.850
I said because 24-Hour Fitness is a great
gym.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:50.620
They have a lot of great things going on.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:53.959
But I will tell you one thing about why people
join Bally Total Fitness here.

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:58.580
Because we like committed members, because
our members who are close to us, we're located

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:02.170
in a perfect location, we intentionally chose
certain real estate properties because we

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.680
want to save time for you, because we want
you to go home and spend time with your kids

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:06.680
and your wife.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.680
That's important to us.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:08.889
But we still want you to stay in shape.

00:15:08.889 --> 00:15:09.889
Does that make sense?"

00:15:09.889 --> 00:15:11.520
And boom, we got the contract.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.379
So they'd come on board and the contract.

00:15:13.379 --> 00:15:14.630
. . so build other people up.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:17.920
Sometimes you've got to ask, okay, so, tell
me about the competitors, what you like about

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:18.920
them.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:19.920
They do a lot of great things.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:20.920
Let me tell you what we do.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.639
What's more important to you.

00:15:22.639 --> 00:15:26.470
. . And then you self-promote your business
based on what the needs are of the client

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:27.470
out there.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:29.500
#4: Make some predictions.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:31.059
Make some predictions.

00:15:31.059 --> 00:15:33.790
I predict.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.139
. . is going to take place.

00:15:35.139 --> 00:15:36.139
Okay.

00:15:36.139 --> 00:15:41.370
For instance, I just made a prediction a couple
of days ago on a Twitter video and I told

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.089
everybody what my thoughts are on Twitter.

00:15:43.089 --> 00:15:44.240
I may be completely wrong.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:48.769
But I feel based on the research I've done
and the intuition that I have, I feel that

00:15:48.769 --> 00:15:52.519
something's going to happen with Twitter and
there's a reason why their valuation went

00:15:52.519 --> 00:15:57.880
from being a $40 billion company to today
no one even wants to come pay them a $10 billion

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:58.880
company.

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:00.290
Not Apple, not Salesforce, not Google.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.079
They all were interested at one time, no one
wants to buy them.

00:16:03.079 --> 00:16:04.649
So I made my predictions about Twitter.

00:16:04.649 --> 00:16:06.620
If you haven't seen the video, you can go
see the video.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:10.160
The video is titled, Is Twitter the Next Myspace?

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.160
Or something like that.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.490
Let's put a link of it or an image of it so
they can see it.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:19.209
Make some predictions based on your intuition
and based on research.

00:16:19.209 --> 00:16:20.279
Why is that important?

00:16:20.279 --> 00:16:23.190
Well what if some of your predictions become
a reality?

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:25.720
Okay, then you have credibility.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.889
Because when you say what's going to take
place, it becomes a reality.

00:16:28.889 --> 00:16:33.640
Just make sure you're not making things up
based on a nonsense opinion.

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.339
Then you're like everybody else.

00:16:35.339 --> 00:16:38.990
You can't self-promote that because then you're
decisions are not that accurate.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.319
Now some people may say, What dumb advice,
Pat.

00:16:41.319 --> 00:16:43.600
Are you really telling people to make some
predictions?"

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:47.800
Yeah, that's kind of what great real estate
developers do.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.309
That's kind of what great real estate investors
do.

00:16:50.309 --> 00:16:52.009
That's kind of what great stockbrokers do.

00:16:52.009 --> 00:16:54.749
They say, I think this is what's going to
happen with the market and if you want to

00:16:54.749 --> 00:16:56.959
position yourself, I foresee.

00:16:56.959 --> 00:16:58.520
. . taking place.

00:16:58.520 --> 00:16:59.569
So why not you do it?

00:16:59.569 --> 00:17:02.889
Hey, I foresee the economy and the marketplace
going.

00:17:02.889 --> 00:17:05.470
. . in this area and I think you need to position
yourself here.

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:06.740
I think you're smart if you do this.

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:10.630
I wrote a book called The Next Perfect Storm
specifically for the life insurance industry.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:14.490
I'm not recommending you read it, it's for
my industry, the life insurance industry.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:18.180
I wrote the book with the prediction I made
on what I foresee happening in the marketplace

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.190
in the next five, 10, 15, 20 years.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:23.620
All these insurance companies read it and
they wanted to partner up with us.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:24.620
Why?

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:25.770
Because they said, this makes sense.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:30.631
Don't be afraid to make some predictions within
your industry, your own marketplace that you

00:17:30.631 --> 00:17:31.631
have going on.

00:17:31.631 --> 00:17:32.631
Next, name dropping.

00:17:32.631 --> 00:17:34.400
Let me talk about name dropping.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:41.320
There are ways you do name dropping that is
absolutely annoying and it backfires.

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:43.040
It's absolutely annoying and it backfires.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.960
Let me give you the simplest one.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:47.790
Don't namedrop if you don't know the person.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:48.790
Okay.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.910
So for instance, if you say something like,
oh, you know what man, I'm good friends with

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:53.910
Beyoncé.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:54.910
Oh really?

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:55.910
That's pretty impressive.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:18:00.070
Yeah, Beyoncé and I. . . and all you ever
did is you went to a concert and Beyoncé

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:03.310
was there with 30,000 other people, and you
claim you're friends because you're friends

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:06.820
with her on Facebook, because you're a fan
and you follow her on Twitter.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.410
You're not friends, right?

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:10.340
But some people like to say that.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:13.840
Oh, you know, I got to tell you about this
story with.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:20.610
. . if you're going to name drop, do it in
a subtle way, but you better validate it.

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:26.100
People have done that to me and once they
couldn't validate it, it completely lost their

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:27.100
credibility.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:30.880
One of the reasons why I left the former company
is because there was somebody there that kept

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:34.040
name dropping and they never became a reality.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:36.510
Eventually everybody said this guy's full
of it.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.590
I like credibility.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.910
I like for you to say it and it becomes a
reality.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:48.950
So now if you do name drop, for instance,
yeah, you know, John, this is a great opportunity

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.510
to sit down with you and talk to you.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:55.410
You know, one of the things I like is that
you kind of remind me of Steinbrenner.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:59.780
Back in the day I used to work for the Yankees
and when I worked for the Yankees, I moved

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:03.460
up in the company and I started working with
Mr. Steinbrenner and I traveled with him and

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:07.570
his family and it was a great experience,
but you and him have a very similar presence

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:08.990
together and it's great to meet you.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:10.400
I've heard a lot of good things about you.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:11.400
[snap] Okay.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:13.280
There is a connection.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:16.800
Now if he goes back and finds out that never
happened, you lose the deal.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.460
But if he goes back and finds out that happened,
man, credibility.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.460
Come on in.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.460
What do we need to do?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.040
So you call back, and he's always going to
link you.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:26.930
No one's ever going to say it, but you call
back, who's calling?

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:27.930
Billy Bob.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.460
Oh, Billy Bob is the Steinbrenner guy.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:31.610
Bring him in.

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:33.280
So now what if you don't tell that story?

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:35.400
You wasted an opportunity to self-promote.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.860
A good opportunity.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:38.320
Here's another one how to drop.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.250
Instead of name drop, book drop.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.360
What's book drop?

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:48.270
When you're well read, I've ready quite a
lot of business books, and if I'm sitting

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:52.280
there with a meeting, and somebody says something
in a meeting, and I'll say, you know what,

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:55.270
one of the books I read was such and such,
and in this book it talks about this and I

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.690
feel like this is what's going on here with
the company.

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:58.880
And I recommend that book to you.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:19:59.880
And you'll see them.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:04.660
Every time you see them, if they're sharp
they'll go, what's the book's name again?

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:05.660
And you know what?

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:09.010
I remember one time when another topic comes
up, I read a book once called.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:13.610
. . if you can give two to three book recommendations
in a business conversation with somebody,

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:18.050
in their mind, they're linking you to a self-educated
autodidact.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:23.280
You don't wait and you constantly try to feed
information to yourself because you're a self-educated

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.280
person.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.260
Whether you have a degree or not, it's irrelevant.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:28.140
In their mind, you're educated.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.710
They're not saying in their mind that you
have a degree.

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:32.010
In their mind they're saying you're educated
and you want knowledge.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.460
So book drop sometimes.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:34.740
Not just name drop.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:36.560
Book drop sometimes.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:41.630
Next, strong opinions about certain subjects
within your field of expertise.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:45.300
So it's similar to what I said earlier on
making predictions, but this is strong opinions.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.060
It's not necessarily predictions.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.060
You're making opinions.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.550
I don't agree with where the marketplace is
going.

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:52.860
I think one of the mistakes the industry made
was.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:55.800
. . I think they could have done this better
or they could have done this better.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:58.810
This even helps if you have your own blog
or your own vlog or your own podcast or your

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:01.830
own whatever you write, where people are seeing
your thoughts.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:05.510
You know, I wrote this one blog about this
and I can send it to you, you can read it.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:12.320
And this blog, it created a lot of controversy
because my belief in it was such and such.

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:18.450
For instance, for me, four years ago, I wrote
an article why I don't believe home ownership,

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:21.320
home ownership is not the American dream.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:22.860
This thing blew up.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:23.910
Fox contacted me.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:25.260
CNN contacted me.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.260
Everybody contacted me.

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:33.000
The Denver Post, that I think is the #15 publication
in America did a feature on it.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.360
And they sent me the paper and the frame is
somewhere around here.

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:36.360
I don't know where it is.

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:37.360
It's somewhere around here.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.240
If you go type in Denver Post Bet-David.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:44.200
And the whole feature was they came, pictures,
all this stuff, this entrepreneur doesn't

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:45.470
believe in home ownership.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.030
That was my opinion.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:52.760
It created so much controversy just because
I did one video on YouTube saying why, what

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:55.520
the real American dream is, and I said it's
not home ownership.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.480
It's entrepreneurship, right?

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:58.480
Created a lot of debate.

00:21:58.480 --> 00:21:59.650
Share your thoughts.

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:00.650
Share your opinions.

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:03.440
And self-promote those articles that you've
written.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:06.420
Next, have a certain level of certainty on
what you're talking about.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:09.870
People will know the difference between certainty
and somebody who's not certain.

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:12.580
Believe me, it's not that hard to know when
somebody is certain about what they're talking

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:16.160
about.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:20.360
Initially when we started doing channels,
people would say, Pat, do you read a teleprompter?

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.570
Do you have a teleprompter that you go through?

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:24.360
I don't have teleprompters.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.960
I can't speak about these things with you
if it's not fresh here [mind], because I can

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:31.700
store these episodes in my brain and remember
everything I'm telling you.

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:37.090
Just like people can tell if you know what
you're talking about with a level of certainty,

00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:39.090
if you're feeding this thing [mind].

00:22:39.090 --> 00:22:43.920
And the more with certainty you talk about,
your certainty alone is a way of self-promoting

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:44.920
yourself.

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:48.790
Your level of certainty is a level of self-promotion
that you're having.

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:49.790
Next one.

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:52.930
To young and new entrepreneurs, a lot of times,
now people will say, Pat, how about if I'm

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:54.740
a young entrepreneur.

00:22:54.740 --> 00:22:57.890
How do I self-promote myself if I don't have
any victories?

00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:59.420
How about if I don't have anything?

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:02.280
What am I going to self-promote myself when
I'm dealing with some people?

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:03.620
Very simple.

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:08.170
Everybody started off not having anything
to self-promote themselves with, except for

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:10.300
except for the following.

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:16.130
Mr. and Mrs. Jones, there's one thing I could
tell you is, I don't know many people who

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:21.450
are as committed, hard-working, in their trade,
as much as I am.

